# Architecture in code review (Zelkor)

User-level rule `architecture-in-code-review` applies. This file adds Zelkor placement and spec checks. Architecture findings outrank style.

## Placement (before the edit)

If every demo under `examples/` were deleted, would this still belong in the platform for a customer who never deploys examples?

- **Yes** → `charts/zelkor-platform/`, `agents/`, `mcp/`, `images/`, `tests/`
- **No** → `examples/<name>/` or an overlay (`profiles/values-local.yaml`)

`charts/zelkor-platform/` must not reference `examples/`. Tests must not shape the chart.

## Silent decisions that are always wrong here

- Agent or image talks to an LLM provider, SaaS API, or datastore **instead of** Envoy AI Gateway / MCP gateway / the documented ClusterIP
- New public HTTPRoute, Host, or `*.localhost` / `dev-key` default in the shipped chart or image
- Demo graph registered onto platform Aegra (`aegra.graphs`) or a vendor MCP name in `values.yaml`
- Inline Python in a ConfigMap; copy-paste from `vendor/`
- Kind/test fixture baked into `values.yaml` or a template `| default`

```python
# BAD — second egress; architecture is MCP gateway only
resp = httpx.get("https://api.servicenow.com/...")

# GOOD — tool call stays on MCP_URL / gateway backends
# (customer BYO MCP is workspace.tools / mcp.extraBackends, not a platform image)
```

## Spec first

Name the hop, then open the governing file (multi-root `internal/plan/`). No file → update spec + revision history before more code.

| Decision in code | Governing spec |
| :--- | :--- |
| Install / ingress / Helm knobs | `phase_1_requirements.md`, `architecture_ingress_exposure.md` |
| Agent intercept / wrap / graph routing | `requirements_drop_in_agent_contract.md`, `architecture_graph_routing_envoy.md` |
| MCP backends / native wrap | `requirements_native_mcp_servers.md`, `architecture_native_mcp_oss_wrap.md` |
| MCP / Envoy dataplane | `plan/mcp_envoy_dataplane/` |
| Logging / traces | `requirements_platform_logging.md`, `requirements_agent_trace.md` |
| LLM providers / models | Overlay only — `docs/adding-llm-providers-and-models.md` |
| Platform vs demo vs tests | `internal/requirements/dev/examples_and_demos.md` |

## Review output

For each finding: decision, `file:line`, spec or rule, smallest fix (move layer / update spec / delete bypass). Do not auto-fix architecture unless asked.
